course: dictionary
lesson: 15563
title: Surgically: by a surgeon, or very precisely
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Surgically» is an adverb, so it tells you how something was done. Its first meaning is about medicine: something was done by an operation, carried out by a surgeon. «The doctor surgically removed the splinter from my finger» means the doctor used an operation to take it out.
explain: The second meaning is about care. Surgeons work with very steady hands and great care, so people also use «surgically» to describe work that is extremely exact. «The jeweller fixed the tiny clock with surgically precise movements» means the jeweller was very careful and exact.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, read the words around it. If the sentence is about hospitals, operations or patients, it means by an operation. If it is about careful, exact work, it means very precisely. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Surgically» comes from «surgeon», a doctor who does operations.
fact: «Surgically» means by an operation done by a surgeon, as in «The tumour was surgically removed».
fact: «Surgically» can also mean very precisely and carefully, like a surgeon, as in «surgically precise».
fact: «Surgical precision» means extremely exact and careful work.
fact: In news and sport, «surgically» often means that something was done with exact, careful control.
exercise: «The tumour was surgically removed.» What does surgically mean in this sentence? | By a teacher in a classroom | *By an operation done by a surgeon | With a paintbrush | Quickly and loudly
exercise: «The jeweller set the tiny stone with surgically precise movements.» What does surgically precise mean? | Very loud and noisy | *Very exact and careful, like a surgeon | Messy and rushed
exercise: «The surgeon surgically repaired the torn knee.» Which meaning fits best? | Painted over with a brush | Copied onto paper | *Fixed by an operation done by a surgeon | Thrown away and forgotten
test: «The surgeon surgically removed the tonsils.» Which words tell you this was a medical operation? | *surgeon and removed | a and the | removed and the | the and tonsils
test: Which phrase best describes work that is extremely exact and careful? | loud noise | soggy sandwich | *surgical precision | messy pile
exam: Dad says the cut was surgically closed. What does this tell you? | It was never cut at all | It was closed with a cake | It was closed by a bird | *It was closed in an operation by a surgeon
